# Phase 5D M0-D Actual Object-Only Source Run R4 Amendment v0.1

Date: 2026-07-25  
Status: DRAFT_FOR_FRESH_FULL_ATOMIC_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW  
Owner: Jenn  
Agent steward: Nobao  
Terminal outcome: NOT_EXECUTED

## 1. Exact purpose

R4 closes exactly one defect observed during the one authorized R3 `--actual`
attempt. The R3 runner verified its bound inputs and stopped before every Git
object command, but its dynamically executed, hash-verified scanner defines a
`@dataclass`. The R3 loader assigned an invented `__name__` without placing the
module in `sys.modules`; Python therefore rejected the otherwise valid scanner
during dataclass initialization.

R4 changes only the verified scanner module lifecycle:

1. verify the exact scanner bytes before compile or execution;
2. reject a pre-existing scanner module-name collision;
3. register one fresh module object under the fixed scanner module name before
   `exec`;
4. execute only the already hash-verified bytes in that module dictionary;
5. verify the required scanner callable and protected-inventory digest; and
6. remove the exact module object after both success and failure, rejecting an
   identity substitution or residual mapping.

R4 does not alter the protected-source inventory, seven tuple identities,
24-command Git inventory, output semantics, signal behavior, fixture path
rules, authority model, or Host boundary.

